I've written the assessment to session_plan/assessment.md, but it isn't committed: session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so the commit step did nothing and the file is only on disk. Today's probes turned up two new product bugs that have no ticket yet, both confirmed with real API calls.

New bugs
1. `--temperature` breaks every call to the default model. yoyo --temperature 0.5 -p "say ok" on claude-opus-5-5 fails with HTTP 400 ("temperature is deprecated for this model") and exits 1 with no hint. The same happens on claude-haiku-5-5, while claude-haiku-4-5 answers normally. Anthropic's deprecations page says temperature is rejected on Claude 4.7 and later. yoagent always sends it when it's set (provider/anthropic.rs:791). The example config in docs/src/getting-started/installation.md:118 includes temperature = 0.7, so anyone who copies it gets a broken setup.
2. yoyo offers a model that doesn't exist. claude-sonnet-4-7 is in the Anthropic and Bedrock known-model lists and in /model Tab completion, and calling it returns 404. claude-sonnet-4-20250514 is also still offered, though Anthropic retired it on 2026-06-15. After a 404, the "Available models" hint lists both of these and leaves out the default claude-opus-5-5, plus sonnet-5-5, haiku-5-5 and fable-5-1.

Where #1144 stands (the owner's issue filed today)
• Item 1: done in this morning's session.
• Item 2: partly done. claude-opus-4-6 and claude-opus-4-7 on the Anthropic provider already get their real limits from yoagent 0.27.2. On Bedrock, anthropic.claude-opus-4-7 still runs on guessed limits (200K context, 16,000 output). The cause is in yoagent: its Bedrock lookup only checks its fixed preset list, and that list has no Opus 4.5–4.7 entries, so the newer table limits never reach Bedrock. yoyo also still keeps its own copies of some limits: anthropic_output_maximum and the Claude branch of model_context_window_table.
• Item 3: still open. claude-sonnet-4-5 is still offered (providers.rs:95 and :165, commands.rs:159), and Anthropic retires it on 2026-11-30. Bug 2 is the same problem.

Size limits the planner has to plan around
• src/commands_risk_unhittable.rs is 2,036 lines and not on the exceptions list. 14 more lines and the size test fails, which reverts the whole task.
• src/help.rs is 90 lines over its recorded size. 10 more lines and it fails the same way. Any fix for #1127 (shell commands printing /command syntax) will touch it. I confirmed that bug still shows in blame, ast, docs, risk and memories.

Other notes
• #1114's flag-scanning half is fixed (yoyo -p --print-system-prompt now sends the text as the prompt); the half about values is still open.
• The last 4 evolve runs succeeded (the fifth was still running), and the last 10 sessions had no reverts.
• Claude Code 2.1.318 (Nov 4) is mostly polish and reliability fixes, nothing yoyo lacks outright.
• I saved Anthropic's model-deprecations page to yopedia.
